foreign  welcome back to CBS mornings where we've  got soccer on the mind because once  again it's win or go home for Team USA  at the World Cup in Qatar tomorrow  Saturday the Americans will take on the  Netherlands for a shot at the  quarterfinals first time these two  countries will face each other in a  World Cup match and the last time Team  USA made it to the quarterfinals round  was back in 2002 they lost to Germany in  that year Team USA Defender Walker  Zimmerman joins us now live from Doha  guitar Walker good morning  knockout round but really you guys have  been in The Knockout round already  because it was winner go home against  Iran you got the win how are you feeling  now does it change the feeling going  into a game knowing if you lose you're  done  you know you're right we we did have  that experience of having our first  knockout take place in the group stages  uh I thought we handled it really well  handled the pressure had a great game  obviously got the result and so uh we do  have a little bit of practice for these  knockout stages but we're excited  getting closer to kickoff here tomorrow  and uh the group is in in good spirits  and ready to go  Walker we're excited too and I'm saying  all the experts and I'm using experts in  finger quotes to say that Netherlands is  going to win this game you guys are the  underdog here and I always think it's  always good to be underestimated and  over deliver do you what is your  thinking going into that knowing so many  people say ah USA nope they're not going  to make it what's your feeling going  into that does that give you added  energy added boost  a hundred percent you know we've been  The Underdogs before uh U.S soccer is  used to that whole I think it's kind of  what has made our team so special is the  resiliency that we have uh that  competitive spirit that you know every  team before us has had and we feel like  we embody that really well with our  youth with our energy and with our  confidence so we aren't really worried  about what other people are saying we're  focused on the task at hand and that's  to go out there tomorrow and get a  result  so Walker your story is also energizing  uh you were told initially you didn't  make the roster then two other players  fell out and then you were sent to the  starting lineup uh talk to me about your  personal Journey here  yeah back in in World Cup qualifying  um a lot of ups and downs  um but started off in September not  playing not getting called in in October  was a replacement there and ended up  starting and doing well and earning my  spot in the starting 11 for the majority  of qualifiers so it's been a it's been a  fun ride and now to be able to represent  the US in a World Cup it really is a  dream come true and and all 26 guys are  are feeling good about having that  opportunity well Walker you really have  been making a difference uh there's that  great moment in the second half of the  game against Iran a tie would not have  been good enough for Team USA you're up  1-0 Iranians Iran's player gets around  the goalkeeper gets a shot on goal and  then you come out of seemingly nowhere  clearing the shot what did that moment  feel like yeah take us there yeah it was  it was great it's one of those moments  where you're just so into the moment  you're preparing for the worst anything  can happen and just the anticipation to  be in the right place at the right time  and make a play for the team and  ultimately seal the victory for us so  this special is  um you know a moment that I'll always  remember and it's something I can be  very proud of I like right place at the  right time but you got to have the  skills to do that Mr Zimmerman and you  certainly delivered on that can you tell  us how Christian is doing is he going to  play tomorrow do you guys even know that  yet  he's doing great he's in good spirits  um you know everything's day-to-day he's  doing all of his treatment and all of  his recovery but I think he's feeling  good and we'll be ready to go regardless  of what his status is  all your fans here in the US are very  excited we are ready to go we'll be  cheering you on and we appreciate you  giving us a few minutes of your time in  preparation ahead of the game thank you  Walker Zimmerman appreciate it good luck  good luck USA thank you very much

